424
00:23:49,970 --> 00:23:54,970
And here let's say no recipes found for your query!

425
00:24:01,040 --> 00:24:02,423
Please try again.

426
00:24:03,670 --> 00:24:05,380
But now, how exactly

427
00:24:05,380 --> 00:24:08,260
will we actually display this errorMessage

428
00:24:08,260 --> 00:24:10,700
on the parentElement?

429
00:24:11,850 --> 00:24:14,250
So we could do that right here in generateMarkup

430
00:24:15,160 --> 00:24:17,810
and basically check if the array is empty

431
00:24:17,810 --> 00:24:19,293
and if it is so,

432
00:24:19,293 --> 00:24:21,610
then render the errorMessage.

433
00:24:21,610 --> 00:24:23,100
So that would work.

434
00:24:23,100 --> 00:24:25,540
However, we can also do that directly

435
00:24:25,540 --> 00:24:27,310
in the render method.

436
00:24:27,310 --> 00:24:30,543
So automatically, right as we receive the data.

437
00:24:31,770 --> 00:24:34,930
And I believe that is what makes more sense.

438
00:24:34,930 --> 00:24:36,460
So right in the beginning

439
00:24:36,460 --> 00:24:39,020
when the render method is first called

440
00:24:39,020 --> 00:24:41,460
and receives the data for the first time,

441
00:24:41,460 --> 00:24:45,660
we can immediately check if that data actually exists.

442
00:24:45,660 --> 00:24:48,210
So right now, we only simply assumed

443
00:24:48,210 --> 00:24:49,940
that there always is data

444
00:24:49,940 --> 00:24:53,820
and that we can then generate some markup with that data.

445
00:24:53,820 --> 00:24:55,920
But as always, it's a good idea

446
00:24:55,920 --> 00:24:58,930
to check if the data actually exists.

447
00:24:58,930 --> 00:25:02,740
And that is true no matter if we receive a simple object

448
00:25:02,740 --> 00:25:06,100
or if we receive an entire array of objects,

449
00:25:06,100 --> 00:25:09,300
which is the case of the results.

450
00:25:09,300 --> 00:25:11,980
So let's add a guard clause here.

451
00:25:11,980 --> 00:25:14,450
So if there is no data,

452
00:25:14,450 --> 00:25:16,940
then we want to return immediately

453
00:25:16,940 --> 00:25:20,090
and we also want to render the error.

454
00:25:20,090 --> 00:25:22,090
So we can do that all in one line

455
00:25:22,090 --> 00:25:24,440
and this will then still work.

456
00:25:24,440 --> 00:25:26,200
So this.renderError

457
00:25:28,330 --> 00:25:32,360
and we actually don't even have to pass in any message

458
00:25:32,360 --> 00:25:35,090
because we already automatically get the message

459
00:25:35,090 --> 00:25:38,444
from this._errorMessage.

460
00:25:38,444 --> 00:25:41,500
And so in this case, that is going to be this one

461
00:25:41,500 --> 00:25:43,223
that we just specified before.

462
00:25:44,220 --> 00:25:45,560
Right?

463
00:25:45,560 --> 00:25:47,540
Now, however, in this case,

464
00:25:47,540 --> 00:25:49,600
this check is actually not enough

465
00:25:49,600 --> 00:25:52,360
because in fact, we do get data.

466
00:25:52,360 --> 00:25:54,420
It's just an empty array

467
00:25:54,420 --> 00:25:55,430
and so in this case,

468
00:25:55,430 --> 00:25:58,170
we also want to treat the empty array

469
00:25:58,170 --> 00:26:00,340
as though we had no data.

470
00:26:00,340 --> 00:26:03,530
So this here basically only works for undefined

471
00:26:03,530 --> 00:26:05,152
or for null.

472
00:26:05,152 --> 00:26:08,840
But now we also want to check if the received data

473
00:26:08,840 --> 00:26:11,920
is an array and if it is empty.

474
00:26:11,920 --> 00:26:13,570
So we can do that by saying

475
00:26:14,760 --> 00:26:17,340
so if there is no data or

476
00:26:17,340 --> 00:26:20,540
and then basically, if the data is an array

477
00:26:20,540 --> 00:26:22,400
and if it's empty.

478
00:26:22,400 --> 00:26:23,650
And we can do that

479
00:26:23,650 --> 00:26:25,110
by using a helper function

480
00:26:25,110 --> 00:26:27,470
that is on the Array constructor,

481
00:26:27,470 --> 00:26:28,900
which is isArray.

482
00:26:30,580 --> 00:26:31,763
So we can check that.

483
00:26:33,170 --> 00:26:34,790
And so if it's an array

484
00:26:34,790 --> 00:26:39,530
and the length of the array is zero basically,

485
00:26:39,530 --> 00:26:44,530
data.length zero,

486
00:26:44,780 --> 00:26:46,143
well, then in this case,

487
00:26:46,143 --> 00:26:49,200
exit this function immediately

488
00:26:49,200 --> 00:26:52,840
and also render the error, okay?

489
00:26:52,840 --> 00:26:55,680
So again, if there is no data

490
00:26:55,680 --> 00:26:57,640
or if there is data,

491
00:26:57,640 --> 00:26:59,860
but that data is an array,

492
00:26:59,860 --> 00:27:02,040
and it is empty.

493
00:27:02,040 --> 00:27:05,863
So in both these cases, we want the error to be shown.

494
00:27:07,020 --> 00:27:08,353
So let's check that.

495
00:27:11,990 --> 00:27:14,270
So with pizza, it all works the same

496
00:27:14,270 --> 00:27:16,610
because there are results.

497
00:27:16,610 --> 00:27:20,120
But now with this, ha, there are no results

498
00:27:20,120 --> 00:27:23,200
and then we get our error message.

499
00:27:23,200 --> 00:27:25,000
So great.

500
00:27:25,000 --> 00:27:26,200
That works.

